SUMMARY:Museum Makers: Portraits in Blue — An Introduction to Cyanotype P
 hotography
LOCATION:Hilliard Art Museum\, 710 E St Mary Blvd\, Lafayette
DESCRIPTION:Discover one of photography’s oldest printing processes\, led
  by James Billeaudeau. In this hands-on workshop\, participants will expl
 ore the art of cyanotype\, a historic photographic technique known for its
  rich blue tones. Each participant will have their portrait taken and lear
 n how to transform it into a one-of-a-kind cyanotype print using light-sen
 sitive paper and UV light. No photography experience is necessary\, and ev
 eryone will leave with a handmade photographic portrait of their own.\n\nM
 ember Rate: $65 per person\n\nNon-Member Rate: $75 per person\n\nAdvance r
 egistration is required\, as space is limited.\n\nhttps://hilliardartmuseu
 m.org/event/museum-makers-portraits-in-blue-an-introduction-to-cyanotype-p
 hotography/
